(
 '# WindowsToast'
 ''
 'Fires a Windows toast'
 ''
 '## Why'
 ''
 'A user command that runs for a while gets left alone: the user will switch to something else, and'
 'when it finally asks a question, nobody notices that the session is sitting there waiting.'
 ''
 'Although you may use this package for other purposes, `WindowsToast` was created to cooperate with'
 'the `CommTools` packages. `CommTools` is typically used to interact with the user from user'
 'commands: asking for a decision, a string or a number or offer a list for selection. If    '
 ''
 '`CommTools` offers a hook to notify the user: it calls a function of your choosing just'
 'before it waits. This package offers that function for the Windows OS: `WindowsToast.Notify`'
 '           '
 ''
 '## Example'
 ''
 '```      '
 '      ]LoadPackages WindowsToast'
 '      ⎕WSID←''My Project'''
 '      WindowsToast.Notify '''' ''My message'''
 '```'
 ''
 'A toast appears in the corner of the screen:'
 ''
 '```'
 'MyProject'
 'My message'
 '```'
 ''
 'The first line is what tells *which* session wants something from you: the workspace'
 'name, or the last part of the current directory when there is none. The banner stays up until'
 'it is dismissed, and it comes with a sound. '
 ''
 'Windows lists it as "Dyalog APL" under Settings > System > Notifications, so Dyalog''s toasts '
 'can be muted or switched off without affecting anything else.'
 ''
 'For details on how to use it with `CommTools`, see there.'
 '                                                                      '
 ''
 '## Installation'
 ''
 'For temporary usage, load the package:'
 ''
 '```'
 '      ]Tatin.LoadPackages [tatin]aplteam-WindowsToast #'
 '```'
 ''
 'Since it is user commands that benefit most, `⎕SE` is just as sensible a target:'
 ''
 '```'
 '      ]Tatin.LoadPackages [tatin]aplteam-WindowsToast ⎕SE'
 '```'
 ''
 'There are no dependencies.'
 ''
 ''
 'Typically you want to use is permanently via <https://github.com/aplteam/CommTools> for your test'
 'case. For that install it permanently in your '
 ''
 '## License'
 ''
 'MIT, see [LICENSE](LICENSE).'
 ''
)
